# Scope of variables in java
  region from where a variable can be accessed.

# Method level Scope of variables
These are the variables that are declared the method and cannot be
outside the method.

# Block Level Scope of variables
These are the variables that are declared inside the pair of
brackets "{" and "}".
A block of code may exit on its own {   } . and it can belong to an "if"
statement

# Formal Parameters and Actual Parameters
Formal Parameters -> defined during function definition
Actual Parameters -> defined when we are calling the function

Pass by Value and Pass by Reference
Pass by Value -> copies the value of actual parameter.
                 called function create it own copies

Pass by Reference -> Passes the parameter as reference(address).
                     Called function does not create own copy.

Pass by Value example

Static int sum(int a , int b){

}

int x = 10;
int y =20;
sum(x,y)
x ,y are made own copies to pass the value in method
if they are modify in the function then x and y original value
does not change.



